  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Buku Kas Kecamatan",
    "overview": "The interface is a working ledger, not a dashboard of cards. Every rupiah sits in a column, every running balance stays visible, and every total can be reconciled by reading the sheet. Paper and sheet tones replace the usual app chrome; rules do the work that borders and shadows do elsewhere.\n\nThe system is formal, calm, and dense without feeling crowded. Public Sans carries the language of the office; Roboto Mono carries anything that must line up: money, dates, table labels, audit metadata, and the masthead's institutional line. Red is a stamp, not decoration: it appears when a budget is full, an action is destructive, or a page reports an error.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Flat paper sheets with hairline rules and double rules closing totals.",
      "Tabular numerals in a dedicated mono face; amounts align right in their columns.",
      "Square controls, 2px input and button corners, no card shadows.",
      "A red \"stamp\" vocabulary for computed danger states, not for emphasis.",
      "Institutional masthead with the Kubar emblem, fiscal year, and a quiet utility row.",
      "Responsive by stacking the summary band and pos sheets, then letting wide ledger tables scroll."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Red Rule",
        "body": "Red is a signal, not a theme. It belongs to violations, destructive controls, error pages, and the page-title accent; if it appears as decoration, remove it.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Blue Column Rule",
        "body": "The running balance is the only column allowed a tinted background and a blue-grey left rule. It is the reader's anchor, not another data column.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Column Rule",
        "body": "Any number that a treasurer compares down a column uses Roboto Mono with tabular numerals and right alignment. Do not set amounts in the sans face.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Quiet Label Rule",
        "body": "Labels are small, tracked, uppercase mono. They name the data; they never compete with the figure.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat Sheet Rule",
